--TEST--
`idle` and `maxDuration` are `stream`'s two keys alone, and either one on a buffered member is refused while compiling — `rule:http-server/a-streamed-reply-is-bounded-by-idle-and-a-lifetime`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// `rule:http-server/a-streamed-reply-is-bounded-by-idle-and-a-lifetime`:
// `deadline` covers the connection and the head, and a body read as it arrives
// then runs under two further bounds. A buffered call has no such body, so the
// two keys are not in its bag at all — the refusal is the checker finding no
// such option, which is what puts it here rather than on the one deployment
// that wrote the key and watched it do nothing.
string $url = "https://example.test/events";

// Asserted on both sides, because either half alone reads as correct: the same
// two keys are accepted on the row whose body they bound, so a refusal that
// came from `idle` being unspellable anywhere fails here too.
var $streamed = Core\Http\Client::stream(Core\Http\Method::Post, $url, {idle: 5s, maxDuration: 2m});

// And the refusal, on a row whose verb is its own name and on the one that is
// handed a verb: `request` takes the buffered bag, and a verb chosen at run
// time does not make a streamed body out of a call that holds its reply.
var $a = Core\Http\Client::get($url, {idle: 5s});
var $b = Core\Http\Client::request(Core\Http\Method::Get, $url, {maxDuration: 2m});
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0454]: `idle` is not an option of this member
   --> case.nvs:18:39
%A
   = help: the options are: deadline, connectTimeout, headers, followRedirects, retryAttempts, retryBackoff, retryIdempotencyKey, json, form, body, contentType, multipart, identity
%A
error[E0454]: `maxDuration` is not an option of this member
   --> case.nvs:19:66
%A
   = help: the options are: deadline, connectTimeout, headers, followRedirects, retryAttempts, retryBackoff, retryIdempotencyKey, json, form, body, contentType, multipart, identity
%A
error: aborting due to 2 errors
